<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Liberia</h1><p class="st-meta">1822 CE – 1847 CE · capital Monrovia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The settlement founded by the American Colonization Society for free Black Americans at Cape Mesurado, which became the independent Republic of Liberia in 1847.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-colonization-society">American Colonization Society</a>, founded in 1816, aimed to settle free Black Americans in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. In December 1821 its agents Eli Ayres and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-f-stockton">Robert Stockton</a> pressed local Dei rulers, including King Peter, to cede <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-mesurado">Cape Mesurado</a>, and settlers landed in 1822. The settlement was named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monrovia">Monrovia</a> after President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-monroe">James Monroe</a>, and the colony was named <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/liberia">Liberia</a> in 1824.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The society appointed white agents, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehudi-ashmun">Jehudi Ashmun</a>, who organised defence and trade, while settlers gradually gained a role in government. Other societies founded separate colonies: <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bassa-cove">Bassa Cove</a> joined the Commonwealth of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/liberia">Liberia</a> in 1839, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mississippi-in-africa">Mississippi-in-Africa</a> followed in 1842. Settlers, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americo-liberians">Americo-Liberians</a>, dominated politics and trade, often in conflict with indigenous peoples. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-jenkins-roberts">Joseph Jenkins Roberts</a> became the first Black governor in 1841.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Disputes with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> over customs duties showed that a private society's colony lacked standing as a state. On 26 July 1847 the colony declared independence as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/liberia">Liberia</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-jenkins-roberts">Roberts</a> as its first president.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/colony-of-liberia.jpg" alt="Colony of Liberia" width="320" height="196"><figcaption>Image: Helt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Liberia_(1827%E2%80%931847).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1822 CE – 1847 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Monrovia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jehudi Ashmun, Thomas Buchanan, Joseph Jenkins Roberts</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/liberia">Liberia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Commonwealth of Liberia, American Colonization Society colony</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=colony-of-liberia" aria-label="Colony of Liberia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4381 1942 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Liberia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4701 2198L4701 2198M4701 2198L4750 2246M4701 2198L4722 2214"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4701 2198h0M4750 2246h0M4722 2214h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4701 2198h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4701 2198h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Monrovia. <a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=colony-of-liberia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
